{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":80009,"duration_api_ms":127863,"num_turns":7,"result":"","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"df56a05b-fd83-43d0-ad89-35f33e813031","total_cost_usd":0.4555513499999999,"usage":{"input_tokens":1784,"cache_creation_input_tokens":28810,"cache_read_input_tokens":82850,"output_tokens":2657,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":28810,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":135,"outputTokens":6241,"cacheReadInputTokens":375776,"cacheCreationInputTokens":71841,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.15871885,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":1784,"outputTokens":2657,"cacheReadInputTokens":82850,"cacheCreationInputTokens":28810,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.29683249999999994,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"structured_output":{"summary":"All five amendments identify verified mass conservation defects. CleanFilter and SiphonDetritus silently destroy N/C by reducing pools without routing or recording removed mass. Shrimp reproduction creates mass ex nihilo (25 juveniles per hatch with no biomass debit, EggCohort lacks any mass field). Conservation tests only cover zero-DIC-rate defaults, missing the preset configuration that breaks carbon conservation. The budget system lacks any runtime conservation guard in release builds. Each amendment is confirmed by direct code inspection.","votes":[{"amendment_id":"fr-3-d068d62d","decision":"accept","rationale":"Verified at engine.rs:356-360: decomposer, ammonia_oxidizer, nitrite_oxidizer, and comammox biomass are each multiplied by (1.0 - intensity*0.5) with no routing of the removed mass. Contrast with shrimp.rs:483-491 where route_dead_shrimp_to_detritus correctly converts dead biomass via live_biomass_detrital_mass_g() and adds it to fine_detritus_g_total. The asymmetry confirms this is an unintentional conservation violation, not a deliberate modeling choice. The fix (route to detritus or record as explicit export) is straightforward and follows established patterns."},{"amendment_id":"fr-3-05e25271","decision":"accept","rationale":"Verified: ProcessParams::default() sets both DIC rates to 0.0 (process.rs:187-188), while default.toml sets 0.08 and 0.12 (lines 9-10). Conservation tests (budget_tracking.rs:309-372) use TankState::new() which gets the zero defaults. Chemistry.rs:31-47 applies these rates to modify DIC without compensating organic-C changes. The tests thus provide false confidence about conservation under realistic parameters. A comment or separate test documenting this intentional atmospheric-exchange simplification is a low-cost, high-value clarification."},{"amendment_id":"fr-3-c9458760","decision":"accept","rationale":"Verified at engine.rs:342-345: particulate_organics_g_total and fine_detritus_g_total are multiplied by (1.0 - fraction) and the action returns None (no BudgetDelta). Siphoning is a physical export that removes matter from the tank system. The removed mass should be recorded as a classified outflow via BudgetDelta so the ledger can distinguish intentional maintenance exports from conservation violations. Same class of defect as CleanFilter."},{"amendment_id":"fr-3-77e36c27","decision":"accept","rationale":"Verified: shrimp.rs:371-374 adds total_successful * 25 juveniles with no mass debit. EggCohort (biology.rs:8-12) has only count and progress_days fields—no biomass tracking. The spawning function (lines 264-303) creates egg cohorts without debiting parent mass. The budget test at budget_tracking.rs:135 explicitly sets hatch_success_base=0.0 to avoid triggering this path. This is a clear mass creation violation. The proposed fix (model egg biomass as an explicit pool or debit parent mass on hatch) plus a regression test is the correct approach."},{"amendment_id":"fr-3-a030e641","decision":"accept","rationale":"Verified: budget.rs:141 uses debug_assert! which compiles out in release builds. engine.rs:165-170 runs enforce_invariants (which only checks non-negativity and range constraints per invariants.rs:3-188, not conservation laws) then passively stores the tick in the ledger. No tick-level conservation check exists anywhere. Given that multiple conservation violations have been identified (CleanFilter, SiphonDetritus, shrimp hatch), a systematic guard is clearly needed rather than relying on ad hoc test coverage to catch each one individually."}]},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"150024e8-0ed2-450b-9521-b9100c08185b"}
